  Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/material-design-icons/master/symbols/web/volume_up/materialsymbolsoutlined/volume_up_24px.svg

  Path data is byte-for-byte the upstream `d` attribute. The source viewBox is
  already "0 -960 960 960" — the same 960 grid this drawable uses — so there is
  no rescaling here (nothing x40 or otherwise): the glyph is moved into the
  viewport with a single translateY, exactly as `ic_mode_sequence.xml` does.

  Filled white, not tinted, for the reason spelled out in
  `ic_orientation_landscape.xml`: these icons are read by views that set no
  `android:tint`, so each icon carries its own colour, and anything but white
  would disappear against the dark scrim the gesture hint is drawn on.

  Shown while the finger is dragging vertically on the RIGHT half of the video:
  up turns the volume up and down turns it down. The speaker with sound waves
  is the conventional "volume" mark; the muted variants would be the wrong
  picture for a hint that fires while the level is being changed.
-->
